@lucky13 - Agree 1000% about ATLAS and GPS. I almost made a comment about this but refrained. 

No way does a GPS in any form replace a map. They are two distinct but related things, in that a GPS displays a map. Planning a long road trip on a GPS is essentially impossible. 

GPS does NOT render the ATLAS obsolete, or even obsolescent, as the clue says. Close enough for a crossword, but inaccurate in the real world.

@Captain Quahog Of course I don't use a paper atlas. Nor does anyone else I know.

The GPS on my phone gives directions and literally *shows a map* that looks just like what you'll see in an atlas. Did you really not know that this has been standard for many years?

I get that you *prefer* an atlas. But ignorance of what phones can do doesn't discount the huge percentage of people who grew up with technology and are comfortable with them.

@Captain Quahog 

Oh Quahog, bless your heart. If you were one-tenth as wise as you think you are, I wouldn't bother you at all. 

